[
    {
        "content": "<p>This is an awesome project, formalizing a very interesting and quite tersely written article. Ado’s theorem is a classical result in the theory of Lie algebras, and upstreaming it would also bring many valuable supporting results to mathlib, including the Levi decomposition. Good luck with finalizing the proof and upstreaming to mathlib! Starred your repo :)</p>",
        "id": 627052258,
        "sender_full_name": "Janos Wolosz",
        "timestamp": 1790406321
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"763989\">@Janos Wolosz</span>  Thank you!</p>",
        "id": 627102995,
        "sender_full_name": "Miyahara Kō",
        "timestamp": 1790435666
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh, <a href=\"https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCeti/pull/11223\">Tau Ceti completed its formalization of Ado's theorem today</a>.</p>\n<p>In fairness to Tau Ceti, <span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"110087\">Kim Morrison</span>  reached out to me earlier and offered to delay Tau Ceti's work on Ado's theorem for the sake of this project. I told them there was no need, since my goal isn't to beat AI.</p>\n<p>In fact, I'm supportive of using AI in formalization, such as Tau Ceti and Anthropic's FLT. The reason I'm not using AI in this project is that its purpose is to refactor Mathlib.</p>\n<p>Anyway, Levi's theorem is mostly done. Almost there!</p>",
        "id": 628875404,
        "sender_full_name": "Miyahara Kō",
        "timestamp": 1791031524
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Except one axiom, All is done!</p>\n<p>The remained axion is that restriction preserves Casimir element actions:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">axiom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">restrict_lift_casimir</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">W</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LieSubmodule</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsComplemented</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">W</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hW</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">W</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lift</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">toEnd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">casimir</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">W</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">LinearMap</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">restrict</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">lift</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">toEnd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">casimir</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hW</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">lift</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">toEnd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">W</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">casimir</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">W</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p><a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"116395\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/116395-maths/topic/Restriction.20preserves.20Casimir.20elements/with/628254111\">#maths &gt; Restriction preserves Casimir elements</a> </p>\n<p>If this is proved, Whitehead's first lemma, Weyl's complete reducibility, Whitehead's second lemma, Levi's theorem, and Ado's theorem become axiom-free!</p>",
        "id": 628986953,
        "sender_full_name": "Miyahara Kō",
        "timestamp": 1791093193
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Finally, I did workaround to avoid the Casimir restriction problem, and Ado's theorem (and Whitehead's lemmas, Weyl's complete reducibility, Levi's theorem) is completely proved!! <span aria-label=\"tada\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f389\" role=\"img\" title=\"tada\">:tada:</span> <span aria-label=\"octopus\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f419\" role=\"img\" title=\"octopus\">:octopus:</span> <img alt=\":leanie:\" class=\"emoji\" src=\"https://avatars.zulip.com/3121/emoji/images/47215c07.png\" title=\"leanie\"></p>",
        "id": 629038009,
        "sender_full_name": "Miyahara Kō",
        "timestamp": 1791124020
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/Komyyy/ado/blob/master/Ado%2FGeneral.lean#L20-L40\">Here</a> is proved Ado's theorem!</p>",
        "id": 629038269,
        "sender_full_name": "Miyahara Kō",
        "timestamp": 1791124191
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I want to talk a lot of things, but it's time to sleep. <span aria-label=\"yawning face\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f971\" role=\"img\" title=\"yawning face\">:yawning_face:</span></p>",
        "id": 629039064,
        "sender_full_name": "Miyahara Kō",
        "timestamp": 1791124758
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The change is reflected in the document page!</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://komyyy.github.io/ado/docs/Ado/General.html#LieAlgebra.IsAdo.of_charZero\">Ado's theorem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://komyyy.github.io/ado/docs/Ado/Levi.html\">Levi's theorem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://komyyy.github.io/ado/docs/Ado/WeylReducibility.html\">Weyl's complete reducibility</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://komyyy.github.io/ado/docs/Ado/WhiteheadFirst.html\">Whitehead's first lemma</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://komyyy.github.io/ado/docs/Ado/WhiteheadSecond.html\">Whitehead's second lemma</a></li>\n</ul>",
        "id": 629081440,
        "sender_full_name": "Miyahara Kō",
        "timestamp": 1791149517
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Q&amp;A of <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"579630\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/579630-Project-announcements/topic/Human-powered.20Ado.27s.20formalization/with/629081440\">#Project announcements &gt; Human-powered Ado's formalization</a> .</p>\n<p>Being able to question the author of the code is a privilege that only human-written code has. Feel free to ask anything!</p>",
        "id": 629085368,
        "sender_full_name": "Miyahara Kō",
        "timestamp": 1791152173
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I've created the Q&amp;A thread now:<br>\n<a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"113488\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Human-powered.20Ado.27s.20formalization/with/629093637\">#general &gt; Human-powered Ado's formalization</a> </p>\n<p>Being able to question the author of the code is a privilege that only human-written code has. Feel free to ask anything!</p>",
